# Codeforces Round 1057 (Div. 2)

## D

题意: 一个环形数组, 可以进行任意次操作, 将数组当中元素进行+-1的操作, 要使得数组当中每个元素至少和相邻一个元素相等, 求最小代价

思路: 很容易能想到破环成链, 也很容易想到数组当中相同的元素, 可以看做一个块, 然后又是经典的dp, 但是这样时间复杂度太大. 也是看了题解, 题解提到说每个块的大小最多是3, 同时2和3可以组成任何大于3的整数, 我百思不得其解啊, 现在我有一个很朴素的理解

假设有一个块S长度大于3, 我把它分成两块S1和S2, S1和S2的元素也可以选择和S相等, 但是显然更优的做法是选择S1和S2块中的中位数, 也就是说分块的做法是不劣的, 然后就可以简化这个dp了, 只需要考虑额外两种情况, a[1]和a[n]在一块, a[1], a[n], a[2]在一块

代码:

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
#define ll long long
#define db(x) cerr << #x << " = " << (x) << " "
#define el cerr << endl
#define vt vector
#define rg(x, a, b) (x).begin() + a, (x).begin() + b + 1
#define sz(x) int((x).size())
#define pii pair<int, int>
#define pll pair<ll, ll>
#define pb push_back
#define all(x) (x).begin(), (x).end()
#define fi first
#define se second
#define p_queue priority_queue

void solve() {
    int n;
    cin >> n;
    vt<ll> a(n + 5);
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        cin >> a[i];
    }
    a[n + 1] = a[1];
    a[n + 2] = a[2];
    auto cost = [&](vt<ll> &arr) -> ll {
        sort(all(arr));
        if (sz(arr) == 2) {
            return arr[1] - arr[0];
        }
        ll res = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
            res += llabs(arr[i] - arr[1]);
        }
        return res;
    };
    ll ans = 1e18;
    for (int t = 1; t <= 3; t++) {
        vt<ll> b = {0};
        vt<ll> dp(n + 5, 1e18);
        for (int i = t; i <= t + n - 1; i++) {
            b.pb(a[i]);
        }
        vt<ll> tmp = {b[1], b[2]};
        dp[2] = cost(tmp);
        tmp = {b[1], b[2], b[3]};
        dp[3] = cost(tmp);
        for (int i = 4; i <= n; i++) {
            vt<ll> tmp1 = {b[i], b[i - 1]};
            vt<ll> tmp2 = {b[i], b[i - 1], b[i - 2]};
            dp[i] = min(dp[i - 2] + cost(tmp1), dp[i - 3] + cost(tmp2));
        }
        ans = min(ans, dp[n]);
    }
    cout << ans << "\n";
}

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(0);
    int tt;
    cin >> tt;
    while (tt--) {
        solve();
    }
    return 0;
}
```

总结: 这道题感觉是有一个普遍性质的, 就是一个集合如果可以划分为多个集合, 而这多个集合可以选择与整个大集合一样的答案的话, 但是每个集合又有自己的最优选择方法的话, 这就很显然分块是更优的做法

# Codeforces Round 1060 (Div. 2)

## C2

题意: 给定一个n, 还有长度为n的数组a和b, a是数字, b是代价, 每次可以修改一个a中的元素, 使其+1, 求使得数组当中存在gcd(a[i], a[j]) > 1的最小代价

思路: 一开始呢, 我观察到了, 最小的代价不会超过b[i] + b[j], 因为如果我指定了a[i], a[j], 想要让他们的gcd > 1, 我们分类讨论:

- a[i] % 2 == 0 and a[j] % 2 == 0, 代价为0
- a[i] % 2 == 1 and a[j] % 2 == 0, 代价为b[i]
- a[i] % 2 == 1 and a[j] % 2 == 1, 代价为b[i] + b[j]

从这里我们可以发现, 如果涉及到改两个元素的操作, 最多不超过2次, 剩下的操作就是选其中一个元素使其变成某个质因数的倍数

我一开始在想, 我对于每个a_i, 我去枚举质因数, 然后计算代价, 这样是超时的, 然后我又想着说, 反过来, 我枚举每个质因数, 然后再枚举质因数的倍数, 去找最接近这个倍数的a[i], 这样的时间复杂度, 不会超过max(a) \* log(max(a)) ^ 2, 但是没想到还是超时了

最后看了题解, 它是这样说的, 我们把b从小到大排序, 观察到b[1] + b[x] <= 2 \* b[x], 所以选择其中一个元素, 最多也不会操作超过1次, 除了最小的那个, 所以我们只需要对于a[1]去计算到所有质因数的代价里面最小的那个就行了

代码:

这个是最开始的那一坨, 不过做了很多优化, 时间比较快

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
#define ll long long
#define db(x) cerr << #x << " = " << (x) << " "
#define el cerr << endl
#define vt vector
#define rg(x, a, b) (x).begin() + a, (x).begin() + b + 1
#define sz(x) int((x).size())
#define pii pair<int, int>
#define pll pair<ll, ll>
#define pb push_back
#define all(x) (x).begin(), (x).end()
#define fi first
#define se second
#define p_queue priority_queue

// suppose I want gcd(a[i], a[j]) > 1, and I want to change both a[i] and a[j]
// then a[i] and a[j] can be changed at most 1 times
// if a[i] % 2 == 1 and a[j] % 2 == 1, then a[i]++, a[j]++
// if a[i] % 2 == 0 and a[j] % 2 == 1, then a[j]++
// if a[i] % 2 == 0 and a[j] % 2 == 0, we don't have to do anything
// beside these cases, other cases's solution will be a[i] change k times to reach some a[j]'s prime factor
// maybe I should do it backwards, for a fixed prime factor p, iterate it's multiple and find the closest a[i]
// also I figured out that for the same element in a, I should only care about the element with the lower cost
// the biggest multiple should be 4e5, assume that we have two very big primes p1 and p2, and they are near 2e5
// p1 < p2, p2 want to have a prime factor p1, then we should find a k that makes k * p1 >= p2, k >= p2 / p1
// fuck it's kind of hard to prove that 4e5 is true, but I believe it's true

// after reading the editorial
// if we want to make gcd(a[i], a[j]) > 1, the cost is <= b[i] + b[j]
// let say we sort b, we claim that we only modify the a[i] with the smallest b[i]
// if we choose to modify a[x] more than one time, the cost will be k * b[i] (k >= 2)
// but b[1] + b[x] <= k * b[x]
// so if we want to modify an element more than one time, then we choose element with the the lowest b[i]

const int N = 2e5 + 5;
int new_b[N], lm[N + N];
bool vis[N];

vector<int> primes, minp;
void sieve(int n) {
    minp.assign(n + 1, 0);
    for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        if (minp[i] == 0) {
            primes.push_back(i);
            minp[i] = i;
        }
        for (int p : primes) {
            if (1LL * i * p > n)
                break;
            minp[i * p] = p;
            if (minp[i] == p)
                break;
        }
    }
}

void clear(const vt<int> &S) {
    for (int x : S) {
        vis[x] = false;
    }
}

void solve() {
    int n;
    cin >> n;
    vt<int> a(n + 5), b(n + 5);
    // unordered_map<int, int> vis;
    bool flag = false;
    vt<int> S;
    int mxa = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        cin >> a[i];
        new_b[a[i]] = 1e9;
        mxa = max(mxa, a[i]);

    }
    // for (int p : primes) {
    //     if (p > mxa) {
    //         break;
    //     }
    //     vis[p] = false;
    // }
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
        int t = a[i];
        while (minp[t]) {
            int p = minp[t];
            if (vis[p]) {
                flag = true;
                break;
            }
            vis[p] = true;
            S.pb(p);
            while (t % p == 0) {
                t /= p;
            }
        }
        if (flag) {
            break;
        }
    }
    sort(all(S));
